WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.709 --> 00:00:06.970
Wouldn't it be great if we could simulate
the circuitry of the brain in a way that makes

00:00:06.970 --> 00:00:09.780
us understand what a thought or a felling
actually is?

00:00:09.780 --> 00:00:15.630
Or if we could diagnose diseases early, when
a disease like a cancer is in an early stage,

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:18.350
it's very subtly different from the normal
state?

00:00:18.350 --> 00:00:21.849
How do you tell the difference between an
early disease and a normal tissue.

00:00:21.849 --> 00:00:27.460
Well, with expansion microscopy, we can take
complex systems like cancers or brain circuits

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:31.419
and chemically inflate them until they are
a thousand times bigger in volume or even

00:00:31.419 --> 00:00:32.419
larger.

00:00:32.419 --> 00:00:35.800
So now we can map out the building blocks
of life and how they're organized.

00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:39.750
We can tell you how a brain circuit looks
ideally with enough precision that let's us

00:00:39.750 --> 00:00:42.550
simulate the function in a computer.

00:00:42.550 --> 00:00:46.730
And we've now found that we can actually take
early cancers and tell them apart from normal

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:51.410
tissues which could help revolutionize disease
diagnosis early enough that lets us actually

00:00:51.410 --> 00:00:53.760
catch diseases before they become more severe.

